{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('map.json'))\nm['version']=9\nb5=[b for b in m['behaviors'] if b['id']=='B5-slow-path-accept'][0]\nb5.setdefault('important_branches',[]).append(\\\"the ballot-equality gate returns before the nack branch, so an AcceptReply whose ballot exceeds the round's is never recorded as a rejection; a direct check on this snapshot confirmed nacks 0, accept_oks 0 and no reaction after such a reply (claim C7-accept-reply-higher-ballot-is-a-rejection, confirmed in scope), leaving progress in that situation to the 10s execution timeout\\\")\nb5['unknowns'].append(\\\"the timeout-driven recovery that can also advance a rejected accept round is not exercised by the check, and only the single-reply case was observed\\\")\nco=m['core_overview']\nco['context']['explanation']+=\\\" The same masking holds when the recovering replica is the replica the deployment promoted to leader (IsLeader true, so makeBallot raises the new ballot past maxRecvBallot): the promoted-variant check for claim C6-recovery-ignores-committed-reply-when-promoted confirmed in scope that the committed reply is still skipped and the NOOP vector committed, and the accept handler's own rejection branch for a higher-ballot AcceptReply is unreachable because the ballot-equality gate returns first (claim C7-accept-reply-higher-ballot-is-a-rejection, confirmed in scope), so a rejected round waits for the timeout-driven recovery.\\\"\nco['open_details'].append(\\\"handleAcceptReply returns whenever a reply's ballot differs from the round's, so the nack branch behind that gate never runs and a peer that answers with a higher ballot is ignored rather than counted as a rejection; the direct check for claim C7 confirmed nacks 0 and no reaction, and the pre-accept side has no rejection signal either (PreAcceptReply copies the request's ballot and handlePreAccept returns silently for a smaller ballot), so progress after a rejection depends on the 10s execution timeout rather than on the handlers (S12-handleAcceptReply, S11-handleAccept, S4-execute-loop).\\\")\njson.dump(m,open('map.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nfb={\\\"ref_ids\\\":[\\\"f2523a67a7e94950b0eacff7c280a42a\\\",\\\"374c3ca1233e4a00af8a1f18626ea9db\\\",\\\"B5-slow-path-accept\\\",\\\"B14-ballot-monotonicity\\\",\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S11-handleAccept\\\",\\\"S33-aws-config\\\",\\\"S4-execute-loop\\\"],\n \\\"answered\\\":\\\"Two confirmed results are recorded where they belong in the map. The promoted-leader variant of the recovery finding (claim C6) is added to the core overview's context: with IsLeader true the new ballot is raised past maxRecvBallot and the committed reply is still skipped, so the divergence applies to the replica the shipped configuration promotes. The dead rejection path (claim C7) is recorded in Behavior B5 and as an overview detail: the accept handler's ballot-equality gate precedes its nack branch, so a higher-ballot AcceptReply is ignored, and the pre-accept side has no rejection signal either because its reply copies the request's ballot, which leaves progress after a rejection to the 10s execution timeout.\\\",\n \\\"remaining\\\":[\\\"the timeout-driven recovery path is not exercised by any check, so the delay's actual length in a deployed run is unmeasured\\\",\n   \\\"the scope-issue bookkeeping on the superseded C1 artifact\\\",\n   \\\"the unread helper surfaces (replica/sender.go, replica/mset.go, hook/)\\\"],\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Both results are mechanism-level and belong with the behaviors and the overview rather than in a new map object; the claims and their checks remain the home for the verdicts, and the remaining unknowns are stated instead of absorbed.\\\",\n \\\"understanding\\\":\\\"updated\\\",\\\"question_updates\\\":{}}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Map handoff for the two most recent confirmed results: the promoted-leader variant of the recovery divergence and the dead accept-rejection path. Two objects are clarified with sources (Behavior B5 and core_overview), with no requirement, binding, edge or identity changes.\\\",\n \\\"map_path\\\":\\\"map.json\\\",\n \\\"map_changes\\\":{\n  \\\"B5-slow-path-accept\\\":{\\\"impact\\\":\\\"clarification\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"A branch records the confirmed dead rejection path (ballot-equality gate before the nack branch) and the unknown records what the check did not exercise (the timeout-driven recovery and the multi-reply case).\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S11-handleAccept\\\",\\\"S4-execute-loop\\\"],\\\"preserves\\\":\\\"The slow-path requirement (acceptOKs+1 > N/2), the messages, the accept-phase record contents and the fact relations are unchanged; only the description of one branch and the remaining unknown are added.\\\"},\n  \\\"core_overview\\\":{\\\"impact\\\":\\\"clarification\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The context explanation gains the promoted-leader variant of the recovery finding, and a new open detail states the dead rejection path and the absence of any pre-accept rejection signal, each with its check reference.\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S14-recovery-start-prepare\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S11-handleAccept\\\",\\\"S33-aws-config\\\"],\\\"preserves\\\":\\\"Formation, connection and the existing open details are unchanged.\\\"}},\n \\\"feedback\\\":fb}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-map-c6c7.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-map-c6c7.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
